From 20ed1ea682969d967aff06c73a42a4a62e91c376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:26:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_share_prior_shrink, v2_share_recency and
 v2_partial_game_role_carry (in-season snap-share refinements)

All three were sense-check candidates (2026-10-26) that improved offline next-week share error (WR -4.4% / TE -2.8% / RB -1.3% for
the prior shrink; 1.9-2.9% for recency) and failed the harness bar, 2022-2025 weeks 3-17:
- v2_share_prior_shrink: START-ALL -0.001 [-0.004, +0.001] (bar -0.003), EVERY-ALL +0.001.
- v2_share_recency: START-ALL -0.001, START-TE +0.003 (limit +0.002).
- v2_partial_game_role_carry: part 1 passed (EVERY-ALL -0.006) but the bias moved away from 0 (-0.21 -> -0.27).
Removes the branches, the three helpers, their constants, the last_weight option of expected_snap_share and the two test files.
Default boards identical (.sweeps/board_identity.py: 2023 w3 / w9, 2024 w12, 2025 w6, live 2026 w5 / w9, boards and explanations).
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
